On August 24, 2024, Ken Lill wrote, "I appreciate that you sent me these 3 files, but none of them show me any colors when I open them. I cannot open the .s file."

The .S version of the file is the Z80 assembly language source code of the Astrocade's colors, as the comments say:

// Color Palette for the BPA. 256 entries. Based on Mike J.'s chart
// Assembler version of BPA Palette values. RGB 24bit 8 bit per primary.
// by Steven Scavone, 2024.

It's a plain ASCII file that can be assembled.  I think the AstroCadePaletteTable is meant to be used in another Z80 program to display the colors on the screen.  Additional information about this code and an example of its use would be most useful.

Adam

